description:
Writes a number out in US English words (short scale, up to 999 trillion): cardinal words, the ordinal, and the amount line used on a check. Decimals are read digit by digit. The page at redbison.dev/number-to-words-converter adds copy buttons.

Returns: Text: the number in words. structuredContent { words, wholePart, ordinal, check }.
Example input: {"value":"1234.56"}
